--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

tools/legacy-libs/
    Prebuilt compatibility shared libraries (libtinfo, libncurses, libssl,
    libcrypto) redistributed unmodified from Ubuntu's package archive, so
    that Vivado 2022.2 can run on distributions that no longer ship these
    soname versions. They remain under their own upstream licences
    (ncurses: MIT-style; OpenSSL: Apache-2.0) and are not covered by the
    GPL-2.0 terms above.

docs/img/board.jpg
    Product photograph of the board, from the distributor's own listing.

firmware/src/  (not committed; fetched by firmware/scripts/setup.sh)
    Linux (GPL-2.0), U-Boot (GPL-2.0+) and Buildroot (mostly MIT/BSD, with
    individual packages under their own licences), from
    https://github.com/Xiaozhang-code-cloud/Fish-Wan-plutosdr-fw-7020-SDR

    The diffs in firmware/patches/ apply to that GPL-2.0 source and are
    distributed under GPL-2.0 accordingly.

AMD/Xilinx Vivado, Vitis and any AMD IP referenced by the HDL projects are
proprietary, licensed separately by AMD, and not covered by this repository.
